# TriageBot Conventions

TriageBot is a rule-based issue-triage assistant (severity + labels + owner).
See `constitution.md` and `AGENTS.md` for full context.

## Layering (do not violate)

`app/triage.py` (pure logic) → `app/repository.py` (SQLite) → `app/main.py` (HTTP)

- Put triage/business logic ONLY in `app/triage.py`.
- Keep `app/triage.py` free of I/O: no `sqlite3`, `fastapi`, `os`, or network imports.
- Route handlers in `app/main.py` stay thin — validate, call, return.

## Explainability

Every triage decision MUST populate `reason`. Never return a classification
without an explanation.

```python
# ❌ BAD - no reason
return TriageResult(severity="high", labels=["bug"], owner="backend-team")

# ✅ GOOD - explains each choice
return TriageResult(severity="high", labels=["bug"], owner="backend-team",
                    reason="severity=high (matched 'crash'); labels: bug ('crash'); owner=backend-team (matched 'api')")
```

## The test gate

- Adding or changing a keyword rule REQUIRES a matching test in `tests/test_triage.py`.
- Run `ruff check .` and `pytest` before considering any change done. Both must pass.
